  "query_preview": "..High pressure will retreat eastward over the next \nseveral days, as a long-wave trough forms over the eastern Pacific. \nThis will allow capping to weaken and southerly flow to increase \nacross the region. This is a good recipe for active weather and we \nexpect moderate to high grade Monsoon conditions through much of the \nweek as a result.\n\nWith the active conditions comes more cloud cover and rain-cooled \nair. The warm temperatures that stuck around for most of last week \nwill continue to cool each day, heat related headlines will not be \nneeded.\n\nBy the end of the week and into next weekend, there is potential for \nsome drying, as the west coast trough attempts to move inland. This \ncould bring drier, mid-level air and effectively reduce convection \nover our state. However, if the trough does not move inland as much \nor if it ejects farther north, it may just keep our active weather \ngoing. For now, we have tapered off PoPs a little bit, but we will \nneed to watch this pattern closely, as any change on the trough \nposition could make a big difference.",
